sequenceDiagram
    actor User
    participant App as ProfileScreen
    participant AuthApi as auth.ts
    participant Backend as AuthController
    participant Hash as BcryptPasswordHasher
    participant DB as Postgres

    User->>App: Enter email + password
    App->>AuthApi: loginUser() / registerUser()
    AuthApi->>Backend: POST /v1/auth/login (or /register)

    alt Register
        Backend->>DB: findByEmail (must be free)
        Backend->>Hash: hash(password)
        Backend->>DB: INSERT users
    else Login
        Backend->>DB: findByEmail
        Backend->>Hash: compare(password, hash)
    end
    Note over Backend: Same "Invalid email or password"<br/>error either way — no user enumeration

    Backend->>Backend: sign accessToken (short TTL)<br/>+ refreshToken (long TTL, unique jti)
    Backend->>DB: INSERT refresh_tokens<br/>(SHA-256 hash of refreshToken only)
    Backend-->>AuthApi: 200 { accessToken, refreshToken, expiresIn, user }
    AuthApi-->>App: AuthResponse

    App->>App: setApiUser(user)<br/>setIsLoggedIn(true)
    Note over App: accessToken / refreshToken end here —<br/>never stored, never attached to later requests
